2.  WHY THE NUISANCES CANCEL -- stated as identities, not as hopes
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    gamma_v = v_rel,obs / v_Newton with v_Newton = sqrt(G M_tot / s).  For a proper-motion velocity and a
    projected separation at distance D:   v_obs ~ D,   s ~ D,   so   gamma_v ~ D * sqrt(D) = D^(3/2),
    and   gamma_v ~ M^(-1/2).  Both exponents are the SAME in the parallel and perpendicular bins, because the
    bins are cuts of ONE population on an angle, so in Q = gamma_perp/gamma_par a coherent error in the mass
    calibration or the parallax zero-point cancels to first order and leaves only the DIFFERENTIAL between bins.
  a coherent 0.04 dex mass error and 0.000 dex distance error move gamma_v by 0.020 dex and Q by 0.000 exactly; only a 30% DIFFERENTIAL between the two orientation bins would move Q, and then by 0.0138
  a coherent 0.10 dex mass error and 0.000 dex distance error move gamma_v by 0.050 dex and Q by 0.000 exactly; only a 30% DIFFERENTIAL between the two orientation bins would move Q, and then by 0.0345
  a coherent 0.00 dex mass error and 0.010 dex distance error move gamma_v by 0.015 dex and Q by 0.000 exactly; only a 30% DIFFERENTIAL between the two orientation bins would move Q, and then by 0.0104
  a coherent 0.02 dex mass error and 0.005 dex distance error move gamma_v by 0.003 dex and Q by 0.000 exactly; only a 30% DIFFERENTIAL between the two orientation bins would move Q, and then by 0.0121
  [PASS] 2a d log Q / d log Upsilon = 0 EXACTLY, and d log Q / d log D = 0 EXACTLY, by the structure of the estimator -- this is the only quantity found anywhere in this hunt with a strictly zero mass-to-light lever   (both nuisances enter gamma_par and gamma_perp with identical exponents and cancel in the ratio; what remains is a differential systematic between two angular bins of one population)

