4.  MUTATION CONTROLS AND THE ALTERNATIVE
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  [PASS] M1 with nu = 1 (Newton, or any dark-matter model, which puts no dark matter on 10 kAU scales) Q must be exactly 1   (nu = 1 gives Q = 1.000000)
  a_0 x 1/4, x1, x4 give Q = 1.0503, 1.1412, 1.2378  -- Q is not a_0-blind, but it moves far less than gamma_v does
  [PASS] M2 CAN FAIL, AND IT IS THE LIMIT OF THE INVARIANCE: Q must still depend on a_0 somewhat, or it would be testing nothing about the scale at all; the claim is only that it depends on the kernel SHAPE weakly   (Q spans 1.0503 - 1.2378 over a factor 16 in a_0, against 1.0330 - 1.1746 over the whole kernel family at fixed a_0)

